I now have the complete picture. Here is my report.

## Overview

This is a Spring PetClinic REST application with a parallel OfficeFloor implementation. All owner-creation business logic lives as small single-responsibility "function" classes in `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`, wired into a pipeline by `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Identity/duplicate detection is one stage in that pipeline.

Important: there is a version mismatch between the current implementation and the tests/OpenAPI spec (details in the last section). The implementation is "v1"; the acceptance test and OpenAScPI describe a "v2" (SHA-256 + soundex).

## 1. identityKey / identity key computation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerIdentity.java`
- The canonical identity key. Current implementation returns a plain pipe-delimited string, NOT a hash:
```java
// line 41-46
private static String of(String telephone, String email) {
    String normalizedTelephone = TelephoneNormalizer.toE164(telephone);
    String normalizedEmail = (email == null) ? "" : email.trim().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    // householdId component is empty: a household does not individuate a person (see class doc).
    return (normalizedTelephone == null ? "" : normalizedTelephone) + '|' + normalizedEmail + '|';
}
```
- Key shape: `normalizedTelephone + '|' + email + '|'` (trailing empty householdId component). Telephone normalized via `TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`, email lower-cased.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignIdentityKey.java`
- Pipeline step: `owner.setIdentityKey(OwnerIdentity.of(owner));` (line 15). Wired as stage `assignIdentityKey` in the POST pipeline.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
- Field `identityKey` (line 90-91, column `identity_key`); getter/setter lines 244-250. Also holds `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `householdSize`, `membershipLevelCap`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `deleted`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Sha256.java`
- Shared SHA-256 → lower-case hex helper (`hex(String)`), used by `HouseholdKey` and `CustomerCode`. Note: NOT currently used by `OwnerIdentity`.

## 2. Duplicate detection (409, "duplicate")

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`
- The single hard duplicate check. Iterates all owners, skips soft-deleted, throws on exact identity-key equality:
```java
// line 24-32
String identityKey = OwnerIdentity.of(request);
for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
    if (existing.isDeleted()) {
        continue; // a soft-deleted owner no longer blocks a matching identity
    }
    if (identityKey.equals(OwnerIdentity.of(existing))) {
        throw new DuplicateIdentityException(identityKey);
    }
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java`
- Carries the conflicting `identityKey`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java`
- Responds `409 CONFLICT` with a ProblemDetail and sets property `identityKey` (lines 13-16).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException.yml`
- Registers the handler.

Pipeline: `ensureUniqueIdentity` stage in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (lines 50-53), running after email-domain validation and before capacity checks.

## 3. Soft match / possible-duplicate (household collision)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`
- Marks (does NOT reject) a soft duplicate — an owner sharing an existing owner's `householdId`. Sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. A declared household member (`request.getSharesHousehold() == true`) is skipped, as is a blank postcode:
```java
// line 27-45
owner.setPossibleDuplicate(false);
owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(null);
if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) { return; }
String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) { return; }
String householdId = owner.getHouseholdId();
for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
    if (householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId())) {
        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(true);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(existing.getId());
        return;
    }
}
```
- Pipeline stage `flagPossibleDuplicate` (owners.POST.yml lines 110-113), runs after `flagBulkSignup`, before `save`.
- Note: this loop does NOT skip soft-deleted owners (unlike EnsureUniqueIdentity and CapMembershipLevel).

## 4. Postcode matching

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerPostcode.java`
- Optional postcode; if present must be valid for the city via `Postcodes.isValidForCity`, else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Postcodes.java`
- 4-digit pattern (line 15), region ranges NSW 2000-2099 / VIC 3000-3099 / QLD 4000-4099 (lines 18-21). Methods `isWellFormed`, `regionOf`, `regionCode`, `isValidForCity`. Unknown regions accept any 4-digit postcode.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/InvalidPostcodeException.java` and `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` (400 response).

## 5. Email-domain blocklist

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateEmailDomain.java`
- Hard-coded blocklist and rejection:
```java
// line 18-29
private static final Set<String> BLOCKED_DOMAINS =
        Set.of("mailinator.com", "tempmail.com", "guerrillamail.com");
...
String domain = email.substring(email.indexOf('@') + 1).toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
if (BLOCKED_DOMAINS.contains(domain)) {
    throw new DisposableEmailDomainException(email);
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` + `DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` (400, property `rejectedValue`). Pipeline stage `validateEmailDomain` (owners.POST.yml lines 45-48).

## 6. householdId computation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/HouseholdKey.java`
- Household key = normalized last name (`trim`, collapse whitespace, lower-case) + `'|'` + postcode verbatim (lines 21-23). `id()` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 of the key (lines 31-33). Based on last name + postcode.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdId.java`
- `owner.setHouseholdId(HouseholdKey.id(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()));` (line 15). Pipeline stage `assignHousehold` (owners.POST.yml lines 80-83).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CountHouseholdMembers.java`
- Counts owners sharing `householdId` (stored as `householdSize`). Does not skip soft-deleted.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CapMembershipLevel.java`
- Caps membership level at 1 above the max among existing household members; skips soft-deleted owners (lines 26-28).

Related but name-only (not household): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CountNamesakes.java` counts owners with same first+last name.

## 7. "Flagged deleted" / soft-deleted owners

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`
- Soft-delete: `owner.setDeleted(true); ownerRepository.save(owner);`. Row retained. Pipeline: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml` (load → delete → respond 204).

`Owner.java` field `deleted` (line 99-100), `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()` (lines 270-276).
- Consumed by `EnsureUniqueIdentity` (skips deleted) and `CapMembershipLevel` (skips deleted). Note `FlagPossibleDuplicate` and `CountHouseholdMembers` do NOT skip deleted owners.

## 8. Soundex

- No soundex implementation exists in source. `grep -rni soundex src` matches only a comment in the acceptance test. No `commons-codec`/soundex dependency in `pom.xml`.

## Tests

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
- Two tests: `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserts the returned `identityKey` matches `[0-9a-f]{64}` (a 64-char SHA-256 hex); `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` posts two identical owners and expects `409 CONFLICT`.
- Header comment (lines 9-11): "identity-key-v2: identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))".

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`
- Black-box MockMvc base. Includes `deleteOwner(id)` (soft-delete helper, lines 195-197), `structuredOwner()` (addressLine1 + postcode 2000), `sha256hex`/`shaHex` helpers (lines 282-299), pinned region/postcode reference data (lines 228-237).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — audit test helper (not identity-specific).

Schema/spec references: `possible_duplicate`/`possible_duplicate_of` columns in all `src/main/resources/db/*/schema.sql`; `identity_key`, `household_id` columns there too. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines ~2096-2206 document `sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`.

## Key discrepancy (the "complete picture" caveat)

There are three inconsistent definitions of identityKey / household duplicate handling in the repo:

1. Implementation (`OwnerIdentity.java`): identityKey = plain string `normalizedTelephone|email|` (empty household component). No hashing, no soundex. Household collisions are only flagged (`FlagPossibleDuplicate`), never rejected.

2. OpenAPI (`openapi.yml` lines 2163-2170): identityKey = `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId` (example shows tel|email|64-hex-household). Also states (lines 2189-2194) a "household collision (same last name and postcode) is now rejected as a 409 unless the owner declares sharesHousehold" — which contradicts the current `EnsureUniqueIdentity` (which ignores household entirely) and `FlagPossibleDuplicate` (which never rejects). The `sharesHousehold` write-only field (lines 2096-2105) is read only by `FlagPossibleDuplicate`, not by any 409 gate.

3. Acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.java`): expects identityKey = SHA-256 hex (64 chars) over `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`.

As written, `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` would fail against the current implementation (it produces `+61...|email|`, not a 64-char hex). The code appears mid-migration from a v1 (pipe-string, tel+email identity, no soundex, household only "soft"-flagged) toward a v2 (SHA-256 hex, soundex(lastName) in the key, household collision as hard 409). No soundex code and no SHA hashing of the identity key currently exist.

